#proof[
  A nontrivial nonparabolic subgroup of a torsion-free relatively hyperbolic group contains a loxodromic element. Compare long paths in the two embedded groups tending to its two endpoints. The central comparison in Lemma 88 gives paired frame points $b in B$ and $g c in g C$ with $b^(- 1) g c$ in a fixed finite list. This is a representative of $B g C$. The list is independent of $g$, because only central comparison constants are used, not the remote endpoint connectors. ◻
